  "response": "The best triage order is driven by connectivity first, then size. Several `large_function` findings overlap structurally, so they should be treated as one refactor rather than separate jobs.\n\n1. `src/utils.ts` — first, but incrementally\n\n   This is the broadest dependency bottleneck: **fan-in 18, fan-out 1**, exceeding even the reported p99 fan-in cutoff of 10. It is also a **424-line large file**. Changes can affect 18 direct and 29 transitive importers.\n\n   Split cohesive utilities into focused modules, initially retaining `src/utils.ts` as a compatibility facade. Migrate consumers in small groups; deleting or renaming its exports in one pass would create excessive risk.\n\n2. `src/index.ts` — second\n\n   This is the largest orchestration hotspot: **fan-in 4, fan-out 17**, far above the p99 fan-out cutoff of 11, and **459 lines**. Its large-function findings are largely nested manifestations of the same problem:\n\n   - `build`: 293 lines\n   - anonymous callback inside `build`: 274 lines\n   - `mainTasks`: 194 lines\n   - `normalizeOptions`: 96 lines\n   - `buildAll`: 75 lines\n   - `startWatcher`: 79 lines\n\n   Extract option normalization, build execution, multi-entry coordination, and watcher lifecycle into separate internal modules. Keep `src/index.ts` as a stable public orchestrator. Reducing its 17 outgoing dependencies should materially shrink the context and failure surface of future changes.\n\n3. `src/esbuild/index.ts` — third\n\n   It has **fan-in 1, fan-out 11**, exactly the p99 fan-out cutoff, while `runEsbuild` is **237 lines**, four times its 60-line threshold.\n\n   This is a strong extraction candidate because one importer means its external boundary is narrow, while its 11 dependencies show excessive internal coordination. Split plugin assembly, option translation, build execution, and result handling behind the existing `runEsbuild` contract.\n\n4. `src/plugin.ts` — fourth, with API preservation\n\n   This file has **fan-in 10, fan-out 3** and 29 transitive importers. `buildFinished` is also 103 lines.\n\n   Extract private implementation helpers, but preserve the exported plugin contract. Its high fan-in makes a public restructuring dangerous; the goal should be to make the implementation smaller without forcing ten consumers to change.\n\n5. `src/cli-main.ts` — fifth\n\n   `main` is a high-severity **153-line** function, but its blast radius is comparatively contained: only **2 direct and 2 transitive importers**, and it did not trigger the connectivity detector.\n\n   Extract argument translation, configuration loading, and command execution into named helpers. This is a relatively safe rehearsal for the more load-bearing refactors, but it ranks below the files whose coupling affects much more of the repository.\n\n6. `src/esbuild/postcss.ts` — sixth\n\n   `postcssPlugin` is 140 lines and its nested `setup` is 126 lines. The two findings describe substantially the same code region. Its reported blast radius is only **1 direct and 7 transitive importers**.\n\n   Refactor it as one unit, extracting PostCSS configuration, file loading, and esbuild result conversion. Do not schedule separate refactors for the two overlapping findings.\n\nFiles I would defer or leave alone:\n\n- `src/log.ts`: **fan-in 9, fan-out 0**. It is highly reused but small and has no large-file or large-function finding. Splitting it would create migration churn without evidence of excessive responsibility.\n- `src/rollup.ts`: **fan-in 0, fan-out 7**. `getRollupConfig` is 122 lines, but the file has no importers or transitive blast radius in this scan. Refactor only when Rollup behavior needs active work.\n- `src/api-extractor.ts`: **fan-in 1, fan-out 6** with an 85-line function. It sits at the p95 fan-out boundary but is less oversized and connected than the first three orchestration files.\n- `test/utils.ts`: **fan-in 9, fan-out 0**. Treat it as shared test infrastructure; address its async-fanout behavior separately, not through a structural production-code refactor.\n- `schema.json`: 362 lines but **fan-in 0, fan-out 0**. A schema is naturally declarative and often benefits from remaining a single artifact; line count alone does not justify splitting it.\n- `src/esbuild/svelte.ts`: its 116-, 106-, and 91-line findings overlap, but it has only **1 direct and 7 transitive importers**. Defer until the higher-connectivity build paths are stable.\n- Near-threshold functions such as `swcPlugin` at 65 lines and `swcTarget`/`terserPlugin` at 62 lines should be left alone absent another reason to edit them.\n\nIn short: first dismantle the shared utility bottleneck safely, then reduce outgoing coordination in `src/index.ts` and `src/esbuild/index.ts`. Preserve stable facades around high-fan-in modules; otherwise a refactor intended to reduce blast radius can temporarily produce the largest blast of all.",
